---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import RothLab from "../../components/RothLab.tsx";
import NextTool from "../../components/NextTool.astro";
import Sources from "../../components/Sources.astro";
import "../../styles/simtool.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Roth or Traditional? (+ the Employer Match)"
  description="Roth or Traditional retirement account? The whole decision comes down to one comparison: your tax rate now vs. in retirement. Plus why the employer match is free money you should never leave behind."
>
  <section class="container wl-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Interactive Tool</p>
    <h1>Roth or Traditional — and don't skip the match</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Two of the biggest decisions in a workplace plan are also the most muddled.
      <strong>Roth vs Traditional</strong> looks complicated, but it collapses to a
      single question: will your tax rate be higher or lower in retirement than it
      is today? And the <strong>employer match</strong> is the rarest thing in
      investing — a guaranteed, instant return. See both, clearly.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container wl-host">
    <RothLab client:load />
  </section>

  <section class="container wl-explainer">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>It's a bet on your future tax rate</h2>
      <p>
        Traditional and Roth are two doors to the same room. Traditional lets you
        skip tax <em>now</em> and pay it when you withdraw; Roth makes you pay tax
        <em>now</em> so withdrawals are tax-free. If your tax rate is the same on
        both ends, the two are <strong>mathematically identical</strong> — the math
        is commutative. The only thing that tips it is the rate:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Roth wins if your rate will be higher later.</strong> Classic for
          early-career savers with decades of raises ahead — lock in today's low
          rate.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Traditional wins if your rate will be lower later.</strong> Classic
          for peak-earning years — take the deduction at your high current rate, pay
          tax later at a lower one.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>A big Traditional balance is partly the IRS's.</strong> Don't be
          fooled by the larger number — you still owe tax on every dollar withdrawn.
          Roth's smaller balance is entirely yours.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>The match is free money — take it first</h2>
      <p>
        A 50% employer match is an <strong>instant 50% return</strong> on your
        contribution, before the market moves at all. Nothing else in investing is
        guaranteed like that. It sits at the very top of the priority list — capture
        the <em>full</em> match before paying down low-rate debt or investing
        anywhere else. Leaving it on the table is one of the few genuinely
        unrecoverable financial mistakes. Educational only, not financial advice.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Sources tool="roth-vs-traditional" />

  <NextTool current="/tools/roth-vs-traditional" />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .wl-intro {
    padding-block: var(--space-lg) var(--space-md);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .wl-explainer {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
  }
</style>

<style is:global>
  .ss-headline {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.15rem;
    padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--color-accent-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-accent);
  }
  .ss-headline-label {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
  }
  .ss-headline-value {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--step-3);
    line-height: 1.1;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .ss-headline-sub {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
  }
  .ss-stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-md);
  }
  .ss-stats > div {
    background: var(--color-surface-alt);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: var(--space-sm);
  }
  .ss-stats dt {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-muted);
    margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
  }
  .ss-stats dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
</style>
